{
  "esm": "0.7.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "ERA5_pl_loader",
    "description": "Pure-I/O data loader for ERA5 ECMWF Reanalysis 5th Generation pressure-level fields. Provides hourly pressure-level atmospheric variables (wind, temperature, humidity, geopotential, cloud, ozone, and derived fields) on the native 0.25°×0.25° global longitude/latitude grid, 1940–present, sourced from monthly NetCDF files.\n\nThis is the loader half of the era5 loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§7; bead esm-3nc.1). It is PURE I/O: it declares its source (url_template), the file variables it reads (with units), its temporal cadence, and its NATIVE grid expressed as a GDD Grid with a geographic (longlat/WGS84) crs descriptor. It performs NO reprojection and NO regridding — those are per-variable concerns of the regridding model (components/earthsci_data/era5.esm), which references this file as a subsystem via {\"ref\": \"./era5_loader.esm\"}.\n\nThe removed co-located blocks: the old DataLoaderSpatial block (crs string / grid_type / staggering / resolution / extent) is replaced by the GDD `grid` (family + crs + dimensions + extents); the old per-loader `regridding` block (fill_value / extrapolation) is gone — regridding is declared per-variable on the model (era5.esm `regrid`). Because a `temporal` block is present, this loader seeds DISCRETE cadence for its variables (ess-v9a.5): the runtime refreshes the file buffers hourly.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/era5.jl:385 (ERA5FileSet, pressure-level variables). Split out of the pre-migration components/earthsci_data/era5.esm (esm-te2e).",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "meteorology",
      "reanalysis",
      "era5",
      "ecmwf",
      "pressure_levels",
      "global",
      "data_loader",
      "pure-io",
      "longlat"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "ECMWF",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.1)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Hersbach, H., Bell, B., Berrisford, P., Hirahara, S., Horanyi, A., Munoz-Sabater, J., Nicolas, J., Peubey, C., Radu, R., Schepers, D., Simmons, A., Soci, C., Abdalla, S., Abellan, X., Balsamo, G., Bechtold, P., Biavati, G., Bidlot, J., Bonavita, M., De Chiara, G., Dahlgren, P., Dee, D., Diamantakis, M., Dragani, R., Flemming, J., Forbes, R., Fuentes, M., Geer, A., Haimberger, L., Healy, S., Hogan, R. J., Holm, E., Janiskova, M., Keeley, S., Laloyaux, P., Lopez, P., Lupu, C., Radnoti, G., de Rosnay, P., Rozum, I., Vamborg, F., Villaume, S., and Thepaut, J.-N. (2020). The ERA5 global reanalysis. Quarterly Journal of the Royal Meteorological Society, 146(730), 1999–2049.",
        "url": "https://www.ecmwf.int/en/forecasts/dataset/ecmwf-reanalysis-v5",
        "doi": "10.1002/qj.3803"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/era5.jl:385 (ERA5 constructor). ERA5FileSet, ERA5_PRESSURE_LEVELS_HPA."
      }
    ]
  },
  "data_loaders": {
    "ERA5_pl": {
      "kind": "grid",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "https://data.earthsci.dev/era5/era5_pl_{date:%Y}_{date:%m}.nc"
      },
      "temporal": {
        "start": "1940-01-01T00:00:00Z",
        "end": "2025-12-31T23:59:59Z",
        "file_period": "P1M",
        "frequency": "PT1H",
        "records_per_file": 744,
        "time_variable": "valid_time"
      },
      "grid": {
        "family": "cartesian",
        "crs": {
          "projection": "longlat",
          "datum": "WGS84"
        },
        "description": "Native ERA5 grid: regular global 0.25°×0.25° longitude/latitude lattice on 37 pressure levels. Geographic (unprojected) crs — the regridding model applies the longlat identity reprojection (ESD reprojection/longlat.esm, esd-47z.1). Migrated from the loader's former DataLoaderSpatial block (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1); the loader describes this grid but performs no reprojection or regridding. Dimension cell counts are resolved from the source dataset at load time; the documented native geometry is lon ∈ [-180°, 180°] (1440 cells), lat ∈ [-90°, 90°] (720 cells), pressure_level = 37 standard ERA5 levels (1000–1 hPa).",
        "dimensions": [
          "lon",
          "lat",
          "pressure_level"
        ],
        "extents": {
          "lon": {
            "n": 1440,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "lat": {
            "n": 720,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "pressure_level": {
            "n": "n_pressure_level",
            "spacing": "uniform"
          }
        },
        "parameters": {
          "n_pressure_level": {
            "description": "pressure_level cell count, resolved from the source dataset at load time (37 for the standard ERA5 pressure-level product: 1000, 975, 950, 925, 900, 875, 850, 825, 800, 775, 750, 700, 650, 600, 550, 500, 450, 400, 350, 300, 250, 225, 200, 175, 150, 125, 100, 70, 50, 30, 20, 10, 7, 5, 3, 2, 1 hPa)."
          }
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "t": {
          "file_variable": "t",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Temperature (K). ERA5 NetCDF short name 't'."
        },
        "u": {
          "file_variable": "u",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "U component of wind — zonal wind (m/s). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'u'."
        },
        "v": {
          "file_variable": "v",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "V component of wind — meridional wind (m/s). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'v'."
        },
        "w": {
          "file_variable": "w",
          "units": "Pa/s",
          "description": "Vertical velocity (omega, Pa/s). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'w'. Lagrangian tendency of pressure; positive downward."
        },
        "q": {
          "file_variable": "q",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Specific humidity (kg water per kg moist air). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'q'."
        },
        "r": {
          "file_variable": "r",
          "units": "%",
          "description": "Relative humidity (%). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'r'."
        },
        "z": {
          "file_variable": "z",
          "units": "m^2/s^2",
          "description": "Geopotential (m² s⁻²). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'z'. Divide by g to obtain geopotential height in metres."
        },
        "d": {
          "file_variable": "d",
          "units": "1/s",
          "description": "Divergence (s⁻¹). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'd'."
        },
        "vo": {
          "file_variable": "vo",
          "units": "1/s",
          "description": "Vorticity — relative vorticity (s⁻¹). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'vo'."
        },
        "o3": {
          "file_variable": "o3",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Ozone mass mixing ratio (kg ozone per kg moist air). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'o3'."
        },
        "cc": {
          "file_variable": "cc",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Fraction of cloud cover (dimensionless, 0–1). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'cc'. Stored as 0–1 fraction in ERA5 files."
        },
        "ciwc": {
          "file_variable": "ciwc",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Specific cloud ice water content (kg ice per kg moist air). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'ciwc'."
        },
        "clwc": {
          "file_variable": "clwc",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Specific cloud liquid water content (kg liquid water per kg moist air). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'clwc'."
        },
        "crwc": {
          "file_variable": "crwc",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Specific rain water content (kg rain water per kg moist air). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'crwc'."
        },
        "cswc": {
          "file_variable": "cswc",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Specific snow water content (kg snow water per kg moist air). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'cswc'."
        },
        "pv": {
          "file_variable": "pv",
          "units": "K*m^2/(kg*s)",
          "description": "Potential vorticity (K m² kg⁻¹ s⁻¹). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'pv'."
        }
      },
      "reference": {
        "citation": "Hersbach, H. et al. (2020). The ERA5 global reanalysis. Quarterly Journal of the Royal Meteorological Society, 146(730), 1999–2049.",
        "url": "https://www.ecmwf.int/en/forecasts/dataset/ecmwf-reanalysis-v5",
        "doi": "10.1002/qj.3803"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "era5",
          "ecmwf",
          "meteorology",
          "reanalysis",
          "global",
          "pressure-level",
          "hourly",
          "0.25deg"
        ],
        "earthscidata_source": "src/era5.jl::ERA5FileSet (pressure-level variables)",
        "native_resolution_deg": {
          "longitude": 0.25,
          "latitude": 0.25
        },
        "native_extent": {
          "longitude": [-180.0, 180.0],
          "latitude": [-90.0, 90.0],
          "pressure_level_hpa": [1.0, 1000.0]
        },
        "native_staggering": "All variables are cell-centered (longitude/latitude/pressure_level all 'center') — ERA5 is stored on a regular non-staggered grid. The model regrids the horizontal wind components u, v with B-spline interpolation and all centered scalars (including the vertical-velocity field w) conservatively (RFC §5.2); see era5.esm `regrid`.",
        "pressure_levels_hpa": [1000, 975, 950, 925, 900, 875, 850, 825, 800, 775, 750, 700, 650, 600, 550, 500, 450, 400, 350, 300, 250, 225, 200, 175, 150, 125, 100, 70, 50, 30, 20, 10, 7, 5, 3, 2, 1],
        "netcdf_dimensions": ["longitude", "latitude", "pressure_level", "valid_time"],
        "file_naming": "era5_pl_{YYYY}_{MM:02d}.nc (monthly, one file per calendar month, all 16 pressure-level variables plus pressure_level dimension)",
        "level_indexing_note": "This loader's pressure_level dimension uses hPa values (1–1000 hPa) matching the NetCDF 'pressure_level' dimension. The regridding model's lev parameter uses 1-based integer indexing (1=1000 hPa, 37=1 hPa) matching the upstream ERA5FileSet convention; the runtime converts lev → hPa using the pressure_levels_hpa table before querying this loader.",
        "access_note": "ERA5 data is available from the Copernicus Climate Data Store (CDS) at https://cds.climate.copernicus.eu/. The url_template above uses a placeholder earthsci.dev mirror; in production, set EARTHSCIDATADIR to a local cache directory populated via the CDS API or the EarthSciData.jl ERA5FileSet download utilities.",
        "cds": {
          "dataset": "reanalysis-era5-pressure-levels",
          "format": "netcdf",
          "description": "Opt-in CDS request descriptor (gap G7). When the loader seam is routed through the EarthSciIO provider adapter (earthsci_toolkit.data_loaders.esio_provider.esio_provider_factory), this block makes the loader resolve to the real Copernicus CDS API instead of the placeholder earthsci.dev mirror: the adapter builds a per-month `cds://reanalysis-era5-pressure-levels?<request>` URL (earthsciio.era5.era5_cds_url) whose `area` is the simulation domain's WGS84 bounding box, whose `variable` list maps this loader's NetCDF short names (t, u, v, r, …) to the CDS long names, and whose `pressure_level` set is `pressure_levels` below (default: all 37 ERA5 levels). EarthSciIO's registered `cds` transport then submits/polls/downloads the NetCDF asset, authenticating with the PRIVATE-TOKEN from ~/.cdsapirc or $CDSAPI_KEY. The submit→poll→download handshake cannot be expressed as the default ESS opener/fetcher's single HTTP GET, which is why the CDS path lives in the esio adapter rather than the default provider.",
          "pressure_levels_note": "Optional `pressure_levels` key (a list of hPa integers) trims the CDS request to the levels actually needed; omit it to request the full 37-level set (large download). For a surface-reduced model (e.g. camp_fire's ground_surface interface, lev=min) set it to the near-surface levels, e.g. [1000]."
        },
        "temporal_note": "ERA5 monthly files are released with a ~2-month lag. The temporal.end above is approximate; update as new months are released. ERA5 Back Extension covers 1940–1978 with slightly reduced quality; the main ERA5 record begins January 1979."
      }
    }
  }
}
